  "goodToKnow": "Die Krippe is a manger or crib, especially die Weihnachtskrippe (nativity scene), a big tradition in Bavaria and the Erzgebirge. It also means a nursery for children under three (Kinderkrippe), before the Kindergarten. Since August 2013, children in Germany have a legal right to a childcare place from their first birthday, although places are often scarce. Plural: die Krippen."
